                <pb facs="0103" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890b.6363 Gulf Oil Corporation/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain (Atherton) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-30T12:00:00+00:00">March 30,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 30—7:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>123. I delivered note (Department’s telegram 100, March 26, 4 p.m.) to Sir John
                    Simon this morning who asked me to assure you the matter was receiving his
                    attention and memoranda for a draft reply had already been compiled. The British
                    position will be discussed at the next Cabinet meeting which takes place on
                    April 6th and Sir John stated he hoped immediately thereafter to forward me a
                    note of reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
